{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OBSOLETE / superseded by closed 744a-d299-970b-4140. Investigated while executing epic REB-2658.\n\nFindings (verified against current origin/main @ 2af5a4c773):\n- 273a's motivating problem was 'dispatch_one.py is 796/800 LOC, only 4 lines headroom, so the sibling outbound story cannot land until this file has room.' That headroom now EXISTS: 744a ('Graduate dispatch_one.py off module-size gate') is CLOSED and already extracted the update_one apply phases into dispatch_apply_phases.py. dispatch_one.py is now 673 LOC (127 lines under the 800 cap).\n- The plan is materially stale: it targets 'lines 432-796' and a locally-defined _update_one_dispatch_links; in current code the file ends at 673 and _update_one_dispatch_links lives in dispatch_apply_phases.py:546 (dispatch_one only re-exports it). The complexity-baseline.json key the plan says to re-key (dispatch_one.py::_update_one_dispatch_links) no longer exists (only create_one:36 remains). A new consumer (test_peer_confirmations_store.py) now calls dispatch_one._update_one_dispatch_links, which the plan's 'exactly one test file edited' AC does not account for.\n- rebar review-plan flags: 273a duplicates 744a (shared dispatch_one.py, conf 0.82).\n- The dependent d19d records file_impact=dispatch_one.py (NOT dispatch_update.py) and edits update_one in place; it does not need a dispatch_update.py seam. Its depends_on 273a edge was purely the (now-satisfied) headroom rationale.\n\nDisposition: obsolete. Not implementing a duplicate split that a reviewer would reject. Linking duplicates 744a; unblocking d19d."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786653620916960001,"uuid":"7348b86c-2a3a-4048-8521-5ca0ed9d53c4"}